.TH SYSTEMD\-RECALLD.SERVICE 8 "2026-03-23" "systemd-recalld 0.1.0" "System Manager"
.SH NAME
systemd-recalld.service, systemd-recalld \- desktop audio and video capture daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemd-recalld
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B systemd-recalld
is a daemon that continuously captures desktop audio and video activity.
Audio is captured via ALSA or PulseAudio, and video is captured via X11
or Wayland display protocols. Captured data is stored locally with
AES-256-GCM encryption and can be queried through the companion
.BR systemd-recall-query-service (8).
.PP
The daemon exposes a D-Bus interface at
.B org.freedesktop.systemd.recalld
for runtime control. Use
.BR recallctl (1)
to interact with it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " PATH" "\fR, \fP" \-\-config= PATH
Path to configuration file. Defaults to
.IR /etc/systemd/recalld/recalld.conf .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
See
.I /etc/systemd/recalld/recalld.conf
for configuration options including audio/video capture settings,
privacy controls, encryption, and storage management.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/recalld/recalld.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/systemd/recalld/
Default storage directory for captured data.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/org.freedesktop.systemd.recalld.conf
D-Bus policy file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recallctl (1),
.BR systemd-recall-query-service (8),
.BR systemd (1)
.SH LICENSE
LGPL-2.1-or-later
